## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/twowayswitchifwired.html
- Summary (EN): Chooses between two inputs based on whether a third input, test, is wired. It passes the selected input to its single output.
- Résumé (FR) : Ce nœud transmet l'une de ses deux entrées selon que l'entrée test est câblée ou non.

- Inputs meaning: ["test: optional. Its wiring determines which input is passed through. It can be a different type from the other inputs.", "first: used by default when test is wired.", "second: used by default when test is not wired."]

- Key parameters: [{"name": "Selection", "meaning": "First Input If Wired uses first when test is wired, and second when it is not. Second Input If Wired does the reverse."}]

- Caveats: ["A test input may look wired but still behave as unwired if it comes from a subnet input or another source that is effectively empty."]

